ngly. I couldn't help it, though, because Leon's mocking lines just did it to me.<br /><br /><br />Raelynn Lawson returned back to her childhood hometown Abelaum and was staying at her parents' cabin to attend college and be independent. Her first night there, she was helping her best friend Inaya at her bookstore and clumsily found a book that was a grimoire. Her friend told her to keep it since she's into the supernatural between going on ghost hunts to having her own YouTube channel. She goes to the old abandoned church to film, hoping for some paranormal activity. But what she was not expecting was to summon Leon, who is a demon that happens to be the guard from school and is known for killing. Leon's master tells him to bring Rae to him to be sacrificed, and he refuses. Leon tells Rae that she is wanted as the next scarifice to awaken a god, and he offers to protect her from the monsters that lurk in the dark. But the one thing that he wants in return for protecting her is her soul. Will she give in and give him her soul?<br /><br /><br /><b>“All the time you’ve spent playing in the dark— is this what you were waiting for? For some evil thing to come take you?”</b><br /><br /><br />There were some side characters that I loved and some that I hated. Let's start with the ones that I hated. There was Victoria and Jeremiah Hadleigh who were so fake and only befriended Rae because they needed her for the sacrifice. I liked Inaya, but she was so blind to what was going on with Rae, but I guess that was partly Rae's fault with not telling her best friend what was going on. I also enjoyed Zane, a friend of Leon's who is also a demon and Juniper (the one he claimed), the sacrifice that got away. We didn't see much of Juniper, but I have a feeling from her small appearance that I'm going to love her. I loved Everly and Callum, though we didn't see much of them and can't wait for their book! <br /><br /><br /><b>“I want you. Irrevocably. But I can’t settle for less than all of you. Body and soul, Raelynn. We demons, when we see something we like, we need to possess it. It’s in our nature.”<br /><br />“You should know that I love you, for whatever that’s worth. Stay alive. Don’t waste that mortal life.”</b><br /><br /><br />What I was not expecting was the chemistry between Leon and Rae because it was absolutely unquestionable. These two were made for each other and would do anything for one another. I loved Leon and his sarcastic, protective, and possessive self. I didn't like Rae but also loved her at the same time. The things that made me dislike her was that she just didn't listen and put herself in danger. The one instance that stands out is that Leon tells her to stay inside while he goes to rescue her cat, and she just had to go outside, putting herself in possible danger. And you guys, when Leon saved her cat because he loves them, had me swooning. My one and only dislike about Leon was him calling Rae baby girl, please don't. <br /><br /><br /><b>“My soul is yours to take, Leon,” I whispered. “If you’re still alive...if you can hear me...it’s yours.”</b><br /><br /><br />This was my first book by Harley Laroux, and it won't be last. I must say that I thoroughly enjoyed this. My heart broke for Leon near the end, but I won't disclose why, so you will have to read it, but before you do, be sure to check the triggers. I'm running to read the next book because I love a good revenge story.<br /><br />~~~~~~<br /><br />Starting off my spooky season with Leon 🖤 Please don't disappoint 🤞</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">196 likes</span></button></