2 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span><span class="baseClass RatingStar--small"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation"><path class="RatingStar__fill" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3842737522">April 10, 2021</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Her Soul To Take is a full-length standalone. <br /><br /><br /> I swear, each time the author writes a book, she proceeds her previous work. This book is like no PNR I have ever read. Ever. Add erotica on top it. Now I know what some are thinking it's over the top. I am here to tell you it's not. The author's vivid imagination and her writing talent give you the perfect balance of the two. This book is delicious, and I see a reread in my future. <br /><br />My review will be vague. You will see no spoilers. All I will say is read your trigger warning and don't take it lightly. It's not a really dark book, meaning it's not black; on my dark scale, it's a medium gray to gray. The warning is more of the kinks involved in this book. <br /><br /> Rae returns to live in her birthplace after her parents move to Spain. She dabbles as a paranormal investigator while attending college. Where she first runs into Leon, who is in human disguise and working as a security officer. Leon is instantly attracted to her. And Rae is very much intrigued by Leon. She goes looking into somethings she just shouldn't, and she gets herself into some trouble, and that is an understatement. <br /><br />Rae is what I love to see in a heroine. A strong, independent woman, not ashamed of her sexuality and far from a damsel in distress. Plus, she knows how to ask for help and stands by that person. Leon is the perfect Demon. He pushes Rae's limits and knows when to back off. His comebacks are the best. So sarcastic. <br /><br /><b> “I can’t just keep severed heads around my yard,” I said.  “Oh, I’m sorry.” Leon turned to face me. “Do they not fit your aesthetic? Would death suit your aesthetic better?”<br /><br /></b><p> That was mild compared to his other comebacks<br /><br /> I was all over the place in this book. I went from saying, “ You in danger, girl” (sound familiar ? ) to “I freaking love Leon. “ I just couldn’t get enough and wanted to cry when the book was over. The plot and character growth are astronomical. Parts of this book remind me of Stephen King's early work. And the steam is out of this world—one thousand out of five. <br /><br /><b> Maybe I should put you over that table and spank your ass until it’s a nice, bright, cherry red. Maybe I should make you hold your own panties in your mouth while I do, to keep you quiet. Maybe…” He was so close, his lips brushed my ear, his voice a whisper that slithered into my head and wrapped around my brain. “I should make you spread your legs while I spank you, so I can see just how wet you get every time I leave another mark on your skin.”<br /><br /></b></p><p><br /><br />I can’t wait for the next book in the series and see who and what it is about. If you like PNR and erotica, Her Soul To Take is for yo