758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-3small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-3small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4088340313">July 2, 2021</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText ReviewText--hideContent"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">First of all, there is a good trash, and then there is this. I wish I had buddy read this book because there were times I literally laughed out loud and wish I had someone to talk to about what I was reading. The laughs are the only reason this book gets 1 star (that and you have to have at least 1 start to "rate" a book on Goodreads). Best moments<br /><br />"He took my labia in his mouth, sucking as if it were a meal"<br />"His beauty was dangerous, it was alluring. Like those brightly- coloured poisonous frogs"<br />"I'd gotten piercings before, just not there" &lt;- no shit that's why you're getting that part of your body pierced<br /><br />We start off by finding our heroine "Rae" is a "goth weirdo". We know this because her best friend calls her something similar to that about 3 times in a row. Then to add onto how goth and alt and special she is, the next immediate descriptor is how clumsy she is, and how poor her relationship with gravity is (lol classic). In true fashion she's only clumsy when it doesn't matter, running for her life totally fine no tripping there (eye roll). <br /><br />The whole book we are told, how smart she is. How great of a paranormal investigator she is, but it's all a lie. Rae is constantly upset about other youtubers who fake videos and create "click bait" headlines but the first chance she gets to do something similar she does. She also really doesn't know anything about the paranormal (any investigator wouldn't do what I'm doing....yeah no shit). Throughout the book Leon is constantly telling her, people are trying to kill her and she doesn't believe him, even though he's never lied to her and everything they do is sus. Then when *shock* they try to kill her this is her literal reaction:<br /><br />"Sacrifice, the word slipped past my lips like a prayer, disbelief and pleading wrapping themselves around it. I'm...I'm not...not a sacrifice...I'm not"<br /><br />Also her bad ass demon Leon (aka Killer), is literally the weakest demon we meet in this entire book! Even though he constantly tells us how dangerous and deadly he is. Every time he fights, he gets his ass beat (unless it's killing humans). Archdemon, more powerful then we meet a reaper, more powerful. I'm sorry, but if I'm going to sell my soul to a demon, he better be a kick ass demon, not a weak ass bitch. <br /><br />The FINAL kicker and that these two aren't even the heroes in their own goddamn story!!! Someone else gets the revenge and the next book (two different characters) are poised to take on the big bad. Ugh.<br /><br />Overall, I can't believe so many people are going crazy other this. It's nothing that was promised.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section><div class="Alert Alert--informational">This entire review has been hidden because of spoilers.<div class="Alert__footer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Activate this button to show the hidden review."><span class="Button__labelItem">Show full review</span></button></div></div></div></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goo