mzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn\"}}"},"likeCount":201,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":8},"User:149414829":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":149414829,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1753217872i/149414829._UX200_CR0,77,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":325,"textReviewsCount":155,"name":"April ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/149414829-april","contributor":null,"id":149414829},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/149414829?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4989044833"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.WNeCt1h25MzZCfVAAoU8Zg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.WNeCt1h25MzZCfVAAoU8Zg","creator":{"__ref":"User:149414829"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1775808064255,"createdAt":1695034475330,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1700830161664,"text":"\u003cb\u003e“You’re a light in the dark, and I’ve been in the dark a very long time.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eStarted off my spooky season with Leon, and it most definitely did not disappoint. I went into this not sure how I would feel, but I ate this up. This book absolutely slayed! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHer Soul to Take is the first book in the Souls Trilogy. It is an enemies to lovers, age gap, touch her and die dark romance with drama, dirty talk, banter, and a balance between the plot and smut. I didn't expect to be laughing aloud while reading this, but there definitely were a couple of times, and I was at work making my coworker look at me questioningly. I couldn't help it, though, because Leon's mocking lines just did it to me.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eRaelynn Lawson returned back to her childhood hometown Abelaum and was staying at her parents' cabin to attend college and be independent. Her first night there, she was helping her best friend Inaya at her bookstore and clumsily found a book that was a grimoire. Her friend told her to keep it since she's into the supernatural between going on ghost hunts to having her own YouTube channel. She goes to the old abandoned church to film, hoping for some paranormal activity. But what she was not expecting was to summon Leon, who is a demon that happens to be the guard from school and is known for killing. Leon's master tells him to bring Rae to him to be sacrificed, and he refuses. Leon tells Rae that she is wanted as the next scarifice to awaken a god, and he offers to protect her from the monsters that lurk in the dark. But the one thing that he wants in return for protecting her is her soul. Will she give in and give him her soul?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“All the time you’ve spent playing in the dark— is this what you were waiting for? For some evil thing to come take you?”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThere were some side characters that I loved and some that I hated. Let's start with the ones that I hated. There was Victoria and Jeremiah Hadleigh who were so fake and only befriended Rae because they needed her for the sacrifice. I liked Inaya, but she was so blind to what was going on with Rae, but I guess that was partly Rae's fault with not telling her best friend what was going on. I also enjoyed Zane, a friend of Leon's who is also a demon and Juniper (the one he claimed), the sacrifice that got away. We didn't see much of Juniper, but I have a feeling from her small appearance that I'm going to love her. I loved Everly and Callum, though we didn't see much of them and can't wait for their book! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“I want you. Irrevocably. But I can’t settle for less than all of you. Body and soul, Raelynn. We demons, when we see something we like, we need to possess it. It’s in our nature.”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e“You should know that I love you, for whatever that’s worth. Stay alive. Don’t waste that mortal life.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhat I was not expecting was the chemistry between Leon and Rae because it was absolutely unquestionable. These two were made for each other and would do anything for one another. I loved Leon and his sarcastic, protective, and possessive self. I didn't like Rae but also loved her at the same time. The things that made me dislike her was that she just didn't listen and put herself in danger. The one instance that stands out is that Leon tells her to stay inside while he goes to rescue her cat, and she just had to go outside, putting herself in possible danger. And you guys, when Leon saved her cat because he loves them, had me swooning. My one and only dislike about Leon was him calling Rae baby girl, please don't. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“My soul is yours to take, Leon,” I whispered. “If you’re still alive...if you can hear me...it’s yours.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was my first book by Harley Laroux, and it won't be last. I must say that I thoroughly enjoyed this. My heart broke for Leon near the end, but I won't disclose why, so you will have to read it, but before you do, be sure to check the triggers. I'm running to read the next book because I love a good revenge story.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e~~~~~~\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eStarting off my spooky season with Leon 🖤 Please don't disappoint 🤞","rating":4,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn\"}}"},"likeCount":196,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":73},"User:7215885":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":7215885,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1630275217i/7215885._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1026,"textReviewsCount":986,"name":"Crystal ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/7215885-crystal","contributor":null,"id":7215885},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7215885?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"dark-erotica","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7215885?shelf=dark-erotica"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"dark-romance","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/7215885?shelf=dark-romance"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3842737522"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.3VkteCM-IoAaBYPgvwGCWg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.3VkteCM-IoAaBYPgvwGCWg","creator":{"__ref":"User:7215885"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1783086469781,"createdAt":1616915347091,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1618029662749,"text":"Her Soul To Take is a full-length standalone. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e I swear, each time the author writes a book, she proceeds her previous work. This book is like no PNR I have ever read. Ever. Add erotica on top it. Now I know what some are thinking it's over the top. I am here to tell you it's not. The author's vivid imagination and her writing talent give you the perfect balance of the two. This book is delicious, and I see a reread in my future. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMy review will be vague. You will see no spoilers. All I will say is read your trigger warning and don't take it lightly. It's not a really dark book, meaning it's not black; on my dark scale, it's a medium gray to gray. The warning is more of the kinks involved in this book. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e Rae returns to live in her birthplace after her parents move to Spain. She dabbles as a paranormal investigator while attending college. Where she first runs into Leon, who is in human disguise and working as a security officer. Leon is instantly attracted to her. And Rae is very much intrigued by Leon. She goes looking into somethings she just shouldn't, and she gets herself into some trouble, and that is an understatement. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eRae is what I love to see in a heroine. A strong, independent woman, not ashamed of her sexuality and far from a damsel in distress. Plus, she knows how to ask for help and stands by that person. Leon is the perfect Demon. He pushes Rae's limits and knows when to back off. His comebacks are the best. So sarcastic. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e “I can’t just keep severed heads around my yard,” I said.  “Oh, I’m sorry.” Leon turned to face me. “Do they not fit your aesthetic? Would death suit your aesthetic better?”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003cp\u003e That was mild compared to his other comebacks\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e I was all over the place in this book. I went from saying, “ You in danger, girl” (sound familiar ? ) to “I freaking love Leon. “ I just couldn’t get enough and wanted to cry when the book was over. The plot and character growth are astronomical. Parts of this book remind me of Stephen King's early work. And the steam is out of this world—one thousand out of five. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e Maybe I should put you over that table and spank your ass until it’s a nice, bright, cherry red. Maybe I should make you hold your own panties in your mouth while I do, to keep you quiet. Maybe…” He was so close, his lips brushed my ear, his voice a whisper that slithered into my head and wrapped around my brain. “I should make you spread your legs while I spank you, so I can see just how wet you get every time I leave another mark on your skin.”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI can’t wait for the next book in the series and see who and what it is about. If you like PNR and erotica, Her Soul To Take is for you.\u003c/p\u003e","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1OD0Q29PO9XGD\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.LItgaaLlYi2YsWPn\"}}"},"likeCount":170,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":19},"User:133546057":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":133546057,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1783369618i/133546057._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":70304,"textReviewsCount