u003cbr\u003e▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰▰\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFifty Shades who, said this book, then put poor Christian Grey on its kness for a spanking session worthy of its name. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHoly moly, Harley Laroux. I'll have to send you a fruit basket, sometime in the future, for the service you've done to this community. \u003cbr\u003eAnd by community I mean me. And by service I mean \u003cb\u003eI HAVE SINNED\u003c/b\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHer Soul To Take is so filled with dirty and dark stuff I found myself shrugging and nodding (and also panting a little) at the craziest stuff that happened y the end of it. \u003cbr\u003eYou've got a kink? Raelynn and Leon are here for you with their piercings and giant dildos. You don't feel represented enough as a bisexual person? Scoot over, pour yourself some wine and let Daddy Laroux introduce you to two of the sexiest bi disasters this fictional world has to offer. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eCan you tell I had fun?\u003cbr\u003eI also had one of the worst episodes of insomnia last night, which means I had some time on my hands and basically devoured this. \u003cbr\u003eAnd here's the funniest part. \u003cbr\u003eI may have picked this book up for the smut, but I totally stayed for the plot. I know, right??? I definitely didn't expect this to be so entertaining and bone-chilling as it was. \u003cbr\u003eI was totally absorbed into the story and was kept on the edge of my seat for the entire night. \u003cbr\u003eIt gave off \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/49547508.The_Hollow_Gods__The_Chaos_Cycle_Duology___1_\" title=\"The Hollow Gods (The Chaos Cycle Duology, #1) by A.J. Vrana\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eThe Hollow Gods\u003c/a\u003e vibes, which is another book I totally loved; the whole small town eerie halo, the cult of fanatics, the freaking mystery. It was better than a movie, and Laroux wrote it so well I \u003ci\u003ealmost\u003c/i\u003e didn't care about the kinkiest sex I've ever read about.\u003cbr\u003e(Although it was indeed the dirtiest stuff I've ever encountered in a book. And I'm not complaining, mind it.) \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOn the other hand, I found the dialogues to be a bit stiff at times, and it took me at least 200 pages to finally get into it properly.\u003cbr\u003eI also couldn't seem to notice this seems to have mild anti-religious tones, but I suppose that's to expect on a book where sin personified is one of the main characters. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eRaelynn and Leon's chemistry is on another level. I wasn't fully convinced by their romance, at first, but once they started becoming friends, it was undeniable that these two are made for each other and would do anything to keep the other from suffering. \u003cbr\u003eAnd they would also do anything to each other, if we had to be 100% precise. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1672419439ra/33781984.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePlease, remember to read this book only if you've got a very open mind (basically spread out) and if you're not sensitive about certain topics.\u003cbr\u003eIn case you're like me and aren't easily impressionable and collect kinks like they're Pokemon cards, this can't miss in your collection. \u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1672419007ra/33781965.gif\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e🚩𝙿𝙾𝚂𝚂𝙸𝙱𝙻𝙴 𝙿𝚁𝙾𝙱𝙻𝙴𝙼𝙰𝚃𝙸𝙲 𝙲𝙾𝙽𝚃𝙴𝙽𝚃 𝙰𝙻𝙴𝚁𝚃!*🚩\u003cbr\u003e*𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚋𝚘𝚘𝚔 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚝𝚊𝚒𝚗𝚜 𝚎𝚕𝚎𝚖𝚎𝚗𝚝𝚜, 𝚜𝚒𝚝𝚞𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚜, 𝚌𝚑𝚊𝚛𝚊𝚌𝚝𝚎𝚛𝚜 𝚊𝚗𝚍/𝚘𝚛 𝚛𝚎𝚕𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚜𝚑𝚒𝚙𝚜 𝚜𝚘𝚖𝚎 𝚖𝚒𝚐𝚑𝚝 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚜𝚒𝚍𝚎𝚛 𝚙𝚛𝚘𝚋𝚕𝚎𝚖𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚌/𝚝𝚘𝚡𝚒𝚌/𝚍𝚊𝚛𝚔 𝚘𝚛 𝚘𝚟𝚎𝚛𝚊𝚕𝚕 𝚖𝚘𝚛𝚊𝚕𝚕𝚢 𝚚𝚞𝚎𝚜𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚊𝚋𝚕𝚎.\u003cbr\u003e𝙸, 𝚊𝚜 𝚊 𝚛𝚎𝚊𝚍𝚎𝚛 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚌𝚛𝚎𝚊𝚝𝚘𝚛 𝚘𝚏 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚛𝚎𝚟𝚒𝚎𝚠, 𝚊𝚌𝚔𝚗𝚘𝚠𝚕𝚎𝚍𝚐𝚎 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚔𝚒𝚗𝚍 𝚘𝚏 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚝𝚎𝚗𝚝 𝚊𝚗𝚍 𝚒𝚝𝚜 𝚗𝚎𝚐𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚟𝚎 𝚌𝚘𝚗𝚗𝚘𝚝𝚊𝚝𝚒𝚘𝚗𝚜, 𝚊𝚗𝚍, 𝚠𝚒𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚗 𝚝𝚑𝚎 𝚕𝚒𝚖𝚒𝚝𝚜 𝚘𝚏 𝚖𝚢 𝚌𝚘𝚖𝚏𝚘𝚛𝚝 𝚣𝚘𝚗𝚎, 𝚌𝚑𝚘𝚘𝚜𝚎 𝚗𝚘𝚝 𝚝𝚘 𝚕𝚎𝚝 𝚒𝚝 𝚊𝚏𝚏𝚎𝚌𝚝 𝚖𝚢 𝚎𝚗𝚓𝚘𝚢𝚎𝚖𝚎𝚗𝚝 𝚘𝚛 𝚘𝚙𝚒𝚗𝚒𝚘𝚗, 𝚋𝚎𝚌𝚊𝚞𝚜𝚎:\u003cbr\u003e-𝙸 𝚔𝚗𝚘𝚠 𝚝𝚑𝚎 𝚍𝚒𝚏𝚏𝚎𝚛𝚎𝚗𝚌𝚎 