 on Goodreads). Best moments\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\"He took my labia in his mouth, sucking as if it were a meal\"\u003cbr /\u003e\"His beauty was dangerous, it was alluring. Like those brightly- coloured poisonous frogs\"\u003cbr /\u003e\"I'd gotten piercings before, just not there\" \u0026lt;- no shit that's why you're getting that part of your body pierced\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe start off by finding our heroine \"Rae\" is a \"goth weirdo\". We know this because her best friend calls her something similar to that about 3 times in a row. Then to add onto how goth and alt and special she is, the next immediate descriptor is how clumsy she is, and how poor her relationship with gravity is (lol classic). In true fashion she's only clumsy when it doesn't matter, running for her life totally fine no tripping there (eye roll). \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe whole book we are told, how smart she is. How great of a paranormal investigator she is, but it's all a lie. Rae is constantly upset about other youtubers who fake videos and create \"click bait\" headlines but the first chance she gets to do something similar she does. She also really doesn't know anything about the paranormal (any investigator wouldn't do what I'm doing....yeah no shit). Throughout the book Leon is constantly telling her, people are trying to kill her and she doesn't believe him, even though he's never lied to her and everything they do is sus. Then when *shock* they try to kill her this is her literal reaction:\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\"Sacrifice, the word slipped past my lips like a prayer, disbelief and pleading wrapping themselves around it. I'm...I'm not...not a sacrifice...I'm not\"\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAlso her bad ass demon Leon (aka Killer), is literally the weakest demon we meet in this entire book! Even though he constantly tells us how dangerous and deadly he is. Every time he fights, he gets his ass beat (unless it's killing humans). Archdemon, 